QA6 C2. parse returns a nil pointer with errors.Join(check(a), check(b)),
which is nil when both checks pass: the two operands come from the same
function, and each may be nil. The caller's check of that error does not
remove the typed nil of "return nil, ...", which T returns. (Run time: T(1, 2)
is a nil *E.)
